tgloggerd web application
=========================

The React application behind the tgloggerd web UI. Pages are rendered
to HTML on the server and then taken over by the browser; the design
is in ../../docs/design/web-ssr.md (server rendering and the render
protocol) and ../../docs/design/web-live-client.md (live updates). The
visual design comes from ../mockup.

  - The Go service (webapi/) authenticates, applies access rules, loads
    each page's data and serves the API under /api/.
  - The render service in server/ is a small Node process that turns a
    page's route and data into HTML for the Go service, over a Unix
    socket. It has no database access, cookies or secrets.
  - The browser bundle (src/entry-client.tsx) hydrates that HTML and
    navigates without reloads, fetching page data from /api/page/.

Everything runs through Docker; nothing but Docker is needed on the
host:

    ./dev npm ci
    ./dev npm run typecheck
    ./dev npm test
    ./dev npm run build

`npm run build` writes the client bundle to dist/client (content-hashed
files and the manifest the Go service reads) and the render entry to
dist/server. TGD_BUILD sets the build id both carry.

The API client is generated from the Go service's OpenAPI description
into src/api/generated/ by `npm run gen:api`; until that description
exists the directory is empty.
